From 4f716b2a20b03c8765aece3db3d2c03fd667dcbc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:43:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 160/160] webrender: ES 2.0 integer attributes, textures and
 copies

On an OpenGL ES 2.0 context:
- integer vertex attributes are read without a copy as the unsigned
  16-bit halves of each 32-bit value (two values per vec4,
  <name>_lh0/_lh1), which the GLSL ES 1.00 rewrite declares and joins
  with wr_i32(); a 16-bit attribute fills the low half,
- textures are allocated with glTexImage2D in unsized formats (BGRA
  through EXT_texture_format_BGRA8888, R8/RG8 through EXT_texture_rg,
  float through OES_texture_float, which also holds the 32-bit integer
  data, converted on upload), without texture swizzle,
- uploads are immediate (no pixel buffer objects, no row length: rows
  are packed on the CPU),
- a blit of the same size into a texture is glCopyTexSubImage2D.

wrench reftests/blend/multiply.yaml passes in a strict ES 2.0 context
(Mesa, instancing extensions hidden, every GL error fatal).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
